import graphics.dl
import ../../ui/images.dl

to open native UI image {a pointer to UI image:image} in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set surface to the native UI surface in view
    if surface's decoder's library = (0 as a pointer):
        set surface's decoder to a native UI image decoder
    set pixels to native UI pixels from (the data of (image's path)) using (the address of (surface's decoder))
    if pixels' error's length > 0:
        print line pixels' error
        complete UI image image in view with resource (0 as a pointer) sized 0 by 0 at status 2
    else:
        set texture to a UI texture from RGBA bytes (the data of (pixels' bytes)) sized (pixels' width) by (pixels' height) in view
        complete UI image image in view with resource (texture's resource) sized (texture's width) by (texture's height) at status 1

to close native UI image {a pointer to UI image:image} in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    if image's status = 1:
        release native UI texture in view holding (image's texture's resource)
